    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0493" n="1147" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1147"/>

                <head>No. 548.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Robeson to Rear-Admiral
                    Davis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 3,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith a precept addressed to
                    you, as president of a naval court of inquiry, ordered to convene at the Navy
                    Department on the 7th instant, for the purpose of inquiring into the causes of
                    the foundering of the steam ship Virginius, recently delivered to the United
                    States by order of the government of Spain.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. M. ROBESON,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                            Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Rear-Admiral <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles H. Davis</hi>, U. S.
                            N.,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
